--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,7 +6,14 @@ In-memory inventory service. `api.handle(request)` maps a request
 
 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": <string or null>}`: one
+  page of items, ordered by `id` ascending.
+  - `limit` (optional): integer from 1 to 100, default 20.
+  - `cursor` (optional): the opaque `next_cursor` from a previous response.
+    Omit it for the first page.
+  - `next_cursor` is `null` on the last page; otherwise pass it back
+    unchanged to get the following page.
+  - An invalid `limit` or `cursor` returns 400 with `{"error": "..."}`.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
